From 4f5f6ca76b32334a13a227496ab71e82ba9e6472 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:32:08 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(waterjet): Waterjet Profile operation on a shared 2D
 sheet kernel

Move the plasma contour nesting, kerf ring, kerf and cover laws and
leads, the wire EDM arc-length ring and the open-run offset into
motion::sheet, unchanged in behaviour (a Voice keeps every refusal's
words; the plasma golden stays byte-identical). The cover law takes
several spans per contour and a tab-bridge exemption.

Add motion::waterjet::waterjet_profile: inner-first kerf-offset cuts,
straight or arc leads pierced in the scrap, tabs as uncut gaps with a
led-in stretch between each pair, the tight-hole centre pierce, open
runs on a stated side, optional G41/G42 and arc linearization.

Add OpType::WaterjetProfile (stored id 44) in Section::Waterjet, its
undoable params, .camproj DTO, generation glue, UI page, glyph and
ribbon section; MCP reaches it through add_operation/edit_operation.
Golden CL for a tabbed plate with holes.

Fixes #1883

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
